=== ROOT-CAUSE ANALYSIS OF RESIDUAL DISCREPANCIES ===
1. TABULAR SCALING PARITY (0.0000 Diff):
   All 23 tabular and temporal features (amounts, balances, error balances,
   ratios, log amount, hour of day) are identical to machine precision.
2. GRAPH STATE EVOLUTION:
   Offline batch feature engineering precomputes graph metrics over 72-hour step
   batches (STEP_BATCH_SIZE=72). In contrast, live serving updates the directed
   graph incrementally edge-by-edge per transaction, causing minor degrees/component
   drift as new edges arrive during clean test.
3. REALISTIC LABEL DELAY:
   In online inference, fraud exposure only incorporates historically confirmed fraud.
   Offline retrospective features reflect confirmed fraud up to the batch window boundary.
